<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Static sitemap for the pages that always exist.

  Only canonical short URLs appear here. The legacy .html paths now 301 to
  these, and listing both would ask Google to index two addresses for one
  page and split the ranking between them.

  The homepage section shorts (/how, /faq, /reviews, …) are deliberately
  ABSENT: they are 301 redirects to anchors on the homepage, not pages. A
  sitemap listing redirects is a sitemap that tells a crawler to do work
  and then throw the answer away.

  Service pages live at /s/<slug> and are generated from the database, so
  they are listed here for the nine services that have been live since
  launch; when a service is added or renamed in the dashboard this file
  needs the matching line. A generated sitemap is the eventual fix.
-->
